course: dictionary
lesson: 10883
title: One word, two places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vineyard is a piece of land where grapevines are grown, usually to make wine. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it: «The hillside vineyard was full of green vines in the sunshine.» Hillside, vines and sunshine all point to a place where plants grow in neat rows.
explain: The word has a second meaning in the Bible. In Jesus' stories, called parables, a vineyard is often a picture of God's people or the world. So «the workers in the vineyard» may be a story about people doing God's work, not only about grapes.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. In a geography lesson, the vineyard is a real farm. In a Bible story, read on: the story's lesson shows what the vineyard stands for. Ask: is this about land and wine, or about a story with a deeper meaning?
fact: A vineyard is a piece of land where grapevines are grown, usually to make wine.
fact: Vineyards grow in sunny places such as France, Italy, California and South Australia.
fact: In Jesus' parables, a vineyard is often a picture of God's people or the world.
fact: «Jesus told of two sons» (Matthew 21:28-31): one said he would work in the vineyard and did not, and the other said he would not and then went.
fact: Phrases to know: «work in the vineyard», «the workers in the vineyard», «a hillside vineyard».
exercise: «The hillside vineyard was full of green vines in the sunshine.» What is a vineyard? | A wine glass made of wood | *A piece of land where grapevines are grown | A small church in a town | A kind of river boat
exercise: In geography lessons, which country is a place where vineyards grow? | Greenland | *Italy, a sunny country with many vineyards | Norway, where winters are long and dark | Antarctica
exercise: In Jesus' parables, what is a vineyard often a picture of? | A school for children | A ship at sea | *God's people or the world | A shop selling bread
test: In the phrase «the workers in the vineyard» in a Bible story, what might the vineyard stand for? | *God's people or the world | A bakery where bread is made | A row of houses | A river with fish
test: «Jesus told of two sons: one said "I will go" to the vineyard and didn't.» In this sentence, what does vineyard mean? | A large shop | A kind of boat | *A piece of land where grapevines grow, the place the son was asked to work
exam: Ella reads «a hillside vineyard» and does not know the word. Which clue helps her most? | The word hillside tells her it is on a slope, and the rest of the sentence is about plants | *The word hillside tells her it is on a slope, and the rest of the sentence is about growing plants | The word hill means a mountain made of rock | The word a shows it is small
